# Every text file is LF, in the repository and in the worktree.
#
# Not a style preference - a defence. This desk's global core.autocrlf=true
# rewrote the 22 September batch's 76 files to CRLF during an ordinary
# stash/pop, which put a literal \r inside display-name headings the unit
# suite compares exactly, and JSON the tooling round-trips byte-for-byte
# (2026-08-30; PowerShell's BOM is the same family of wound, HANDOFF's
# environment notes). Every committed blob is already LF - checked with
# `git grep --cached` before this file landed - so this changes nothing in
# the history and stops the worktree drifting from it on any clone.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Pictures are not text, whatever a heuristic decides.
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.png binary
*.webp binary
*.woff2 binary

# Windows batch files are the one text the worktree must keep as CRLF:
# cmd.exe reads a label or a `goto` wrongly across a bare LF, and
# android/gradlew.bat is what a Windows desk builds the app with (2026-09-05).
*.bat text eol=crlf
